<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes van den Bosch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1844">1844</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Van den Bosch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes van den Bosch was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Governor-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>. In 1830 he introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, which forced peasants to devote part of their land or labour to export crops for the colonial government. The system generated large profits for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> but caused great hardship in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>'s colony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-van-den-bosch.jpg" alt="Johannes van den Bosch" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raden Saleh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raden_Sarief_Bastaman_Saleh_-_Johannes_Graaf_van_den_Bosch.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
